.\" man/man1/docv.1
.TH DOCV 1 2026-11-03 "docv 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
docv \- view manual pages and Markdown documents in a terminal, with fuzzy search
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY docv
.OP \-u
.YS
.
.SY docv
.OP \-u
.RI [ section ]
.I name
.YS
.
.SY docv
.OP \-u
.IB name ( section )
.YS
.
.SY docv
.OP \-u
.I file
.YS
.
.SY docv
.B path\-add
.IR dir \~...
.YS
.
.SY docv
.B path\-rm
.IR dir \~...
.YS
.
.SY docv
.B path\-list
.YS
.
.SY docv
.B gen\-cr
.OP \-o dir
.RI [ shard ]
.YS
.
.SY docv
.B text\-worker
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B docv
shows manual pages and Markdown documents in a full-screen terminal viewer.
It reads the roff source of a page itself, with the
.MR man 7
and
.MR mdoc 7
macro packages and
.MR tbl 1
tables built in, from plain or gzip-compressed files, and follows
.B .so
includes.
Files named
.IR *.md ,
.IR *.markdown ,
.IR *.mdown ,
.I *.mkd
or
.I *.mkdn
(optionally gzip-compressed) are read as Markdown instead (see
.BR MARKDOWN ).
.PP
The page is laid out to the width of the terminal, either wrapped or with
each paragraph on one line.
The page header of a manual page stays at the top of the screen and the
page footer at the bottom while the body scrolls between them.
Links can be followed and gone back from: cross-references such as
.MR ls 1 ,
and the links of a Markdown document to other files and to its headings.
Links to URLs are written as terminal hyperlinks (OSC 8).
A dock left of the page holds a search field and the tree of the current
page's group, or of the current folder's pages and Markdown documents; the
field fuzzy-finds in the displayed page while the tree counts the matching
lines of each page, or, after a
.BR / ,
ranks every page of the manual.
The mouse pointer takes the shape of what it is over.
Colors follow the terminal's own color theme.
.PP
A
.IR name ,
with an optional
.IR section ,
is looked up along the search path (see
.BR "SEARCH PATH" ).
A section prefix such as
.B 3
also matches
.B 3p
and
.BR 3type .
An argument that contains a slash, or names an existing file and is not a
section name, is read as a file: a page, or a Markdown document.
Without a page,
.B docv
opens on an empty page with the dock closed;
.B Ctrl\-b
opens it on the pages and documents of the current folder's project, and
typing
.B /
searches every page.
.PP
When standard output is not a terminal, the page is printed as plain text,
.B MANWIDTH
columns wide (80 when unset).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-unwrapped
Start in the unwrapped layout: one line per paragraph, scrolled sideways,
also when
.B start\-wrapped
in
.MR docv\-config 5
is true (the default).
Unfilled text and tables never wrap in either layout.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "path\-add " dir\~...
Add directories of man pages to the search path.
A directory is a tree of section directories
.RI ( man1/ ", " man3/ ", ...)"
or a directory with pages in it.
Each directory must exist; it is stored as an absolute path.
A directory without man pages is added with a warning.
.TP
.BI "path\-rm " dir\~...
Remove added directories.
Fails for a directory that was not added.
.TP
.B path\-list
Print the search path in order, each directory with where it comes from:
.BR project ,
.B added
or
.BR system .
.B (pages)
marks a directory with pages in it rather than a tree.
.TP
.BR "gen\-cr " [ \-o
.IR dir ]
.RI [ shard ]
Generate the man pages of a Crystal shard: the nearest directory from
.I shard
(the current directory by default) upward that holds a
.IR shard.yml .
It runs
.B crystal docs \-\-format json
there and renders two gzipped pages:
.I README.md
as the overview
.IB name .7cr.gz
and the doc comments as the API page
.IB name .3cr.gz ,
with a section per type (and one for the top level when it declares
methods, macros or constants), into
.I dir
(default
.IR man ),
relative to the shard root.
They land in
.I man7/
and
.IR man3/ ,
so
.B docv
finds them as project pages.
A page whose content is unchanged keeps its file and date; generated pages
no longer produced are removed.
A file in the way that was not generated from doc comments stops the run.
.B SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
sets the date of the pages.
.TP
.B text\-worker
Read page paths from standard input, one per line, and write the text of
each page to standard output: its size in bytes on a line, then the text.
The viewer runs these processes to read the text of all pages in parallel
(see
.BR DOCK ).
.SH SEARCH PATH
Pages are looked up, and listed by the page search, along this path,
earlier directories first.
Within each tree, its locale subdirectories (from
.BR LC_ALL ,
.B LC_MESSAGES
or
.BR LANG )
come before it, and sections are searched in the order of
.BR man\-db .
.TP
.B The project around the current directory
The project root is the nearest directory upward that holds one of
.BR .git ,
.BR .hg ,
.BR .svn ,
.BR .jj ,
.BR shard.yml ,
.BR Cargo.toml ,
.BR package.json ,
.BR go.mod ,
.BR pyproject.toml ,
.BR setup.py ,
.BR Gemfile ,
.BR pom.xml ,
.BR build.gradle ,
.BR CMakeLists.txt ,
.BR meson.build ,
.B configure.ac
or a
.BR Makefile ,
looking no higher than below the home directory.
Without one, the current directory is the root, unless it is the home
directory or
.BR / .
The root and its subdirectories are searched four levels deep, skipping
hidden directories,
.BR node_modules ,
.BR vendor ,
.BR lib ,
.BR target ,
.B __pycache__
and symbolic links.
Trees of section directories
.RI ( man/man1/tool.1 )
and directories with pages in them
.RI ( doc/tool.1 ,
or the root itself) are taken.
A page there is a file named
.IB name . section\c
, optionally ending in
.BR .gz ,
whose text starts with a roff control character.
The Markdown documents found along the way, except hidden ones, are listed
by the page search too.
.TP
.B The added directories
From
.BR "docv path\-add" .
.TP
.B The system path
Built as
.MR man 1
builds it (see
.MR manpath 5 ):
.B MANPATH
when set, each empty component standing for the default path.
The default path takes, for each directory in
.BR PATH ,
its
.B MANPATH_MAP
directories from
.I /etc/man_db.conf
(or
.IR /etc/manpath.config ),
or else whichever of
.IR ../man ,
.IR man ,
.I ../share/man
and
.I share/man
exist next to it, and then the
.B MANDATORY_MANPATH
directories.
.SH SCREEN
The top row holds the title (a click on it shows the help), the page's
heading centered, and a close mark
.RB ( \[u1F7AA] ).
The heading of a manual page is its manual and reference, for example
.RB \(lq "ABRT Manual \- ABRT(1)" \(rq;
with the pointer on it, the source and date of the page footer show beside
it, dimmed.
The heading of a Markdown document is its file name and first heading, for
example
.RB \(lq "README.md \- docv" \(rq.
A line runs below it.
Then comes the dock, when it is open (see
.BR DOCK ),
and the page, with the vertical scrollbar in the last column, of
which only the thumb
.RB ( \[u2503] )
is drawn, and below the page the horizontal scrollbar as a line, thumb
.B \[u2501]
on track
.BR \[u2500] .
The bottom row holds messages on the left, and on the right the layout, the
lines in view and the first column in view, for example
.RB \(lq "[wrap] \[u2502] 1\-56/801 \[u2502] col 1" \(rq.
While finding in the page it starts with the selected match and the number
of matches, during a
.B /
search with the number of results; then the progress of indexing and of
reading the text of all pages.
While the help is shown, it shows the lines and first column of the help in
view instead.
.SH KEYS
Text typed while the page or the tree has the keyboard opens the dock with
the keyboard in its search field, starting the field over with that text:
letters find in the page, a leading
.B /
searches every page (see
.BR DOCK ).
Every other action is on a command key.
Keys are looked up by physical key first (the base layout key of the kitty
keyboard protocol), then by the key reported, then by the shifted symbol
without its shift, so the
.B Ctrl
combinations work on any keyboard layout.
.B Esc
takes the keyboard one level out: from the search field to the tree, from
the tree to the page.
